{# Widget "cal" — the month calendar (PL·11), which is the house calendar with
   patrol marks in it.

   THE STEPPER MOVES THE DASHBOARD'S MONTH, not a month of its own. One filter
   drives the map, the log, the charts and this grid together, so ‹ › carry the
   whole question with them and land on the same dashboard a month either side.
   A calendar that stepped privately would disagree with every other card on
   the screen.

   AND IT DRAWS NO FILTER OF ITS OWN. The surface's filter row is already on
   this page (the map and log widgets carry it, once), and two copies of a
   filter row are two answers to "what is on screen". The calendar TAB, which
   has no row, puts the patrol-type chip in the stepper's own line instead. #}
{{ include('@UhifadhiPatrol/_calendar.html.twig', {
    area: area,
    feed: calendarFeed,
    scope: calendarScope,
    month: month,
    now: now,
    previousUrl: path('patrol_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}|merge(filter.inMonth(month|date_modify('-1 month')).toQuery)),
    nextUrl: path('patrol_dashboard', {uuid: area.uuid}|merge(filter.inMonth(month|date_modify('+1 month')).toQuery)),
    controls: '',
}, with_context: false) }}
